{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateParameterExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateParameterExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Real.Irrational"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.ofReebDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.ofReebDecomposition","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L197-L252","doc":"**Existence from Reeb decomposition**.\n\nGiven a weight decomposition `(π_H, π_V)` and categorical Reeb\nderivation `(ξ, θ_A)`, the substrate parameter exists. The\nconstruction:\n\n1. Builds the interpolated differential `d_q = q⁻¹ d + ℏ_q · π_V ∘ d`\n   from the Reeb data (d, π_V) and the parameter q₀.\n2. Validates that the interpolation is well-defined: the compatibility\n   proof `wd_reeb_compat` ensures π_V acts on the same forms as d.\n3. Returns the substrate parameter field `q(p) = q₀` for all p.\n\nThe value `q₀ > 1` must be supplied externally (it comes from\nphysical input — the muon-electron mass ratio in Ch 11). What the\nReeb decomposition guarantees is that d_q is a well-defined\ninterpolation between d and π_V ∘ d.\n\n**Scope warning — the Reeb input is currently discarded.** The narrative\nabove describes a three-step construction, but the term binds `_interp`\nand `wd_reeb_compat` to `_` and never uses them: the result is\n`{ field := fun _ => q₀, … }`, definitionally the same value\n`ofConstant` returns. So this is *not* an existence proof \"from the Reeb\ndecomposition\" — `wd`, `reeb` and the compatibility proof are inert\nhypotheses. Making the interpolated differential actually bear on the\nconstructed parameter is open; until it does, do not cite this as\nevidence that the Reeb data determines `q₀`.\n\nRef: [kock2004] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:substrate-parameter-exists","label":"thm:substrate-parameter-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.kernel_horizontal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.kernel_horizontal","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L195-L195","doc":"**Kernel**: horizontal forms are the kernel of `ι_ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.proj_V_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.proj_V_idem","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L193-L193","doc":"Idempotency of the vertical projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.normalisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.normalisation","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L191-L191","doc":"**Normalisation**: `ξ ≫ θ = θ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.vertical_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.vertical_generator","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L189-L189","doc":"**Vertical generator**: `d ≫ π_V ≫ ι_ξ = ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.contract_xi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.contract_xi","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L187-L187","doc":"The interior product (contraction) `ι_ξ : Ω¹(A) → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.d","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L185-L185","doc":"The differential `d : A → Ω¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.proj_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.proj_V","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L183-L183","doc":"The vertical projection `π_V : Ω¹(A) → Ω¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.theta","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L181-L181","doc":"The canonical 1-form `θ_A`, dual to `ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.xi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.xi","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L179-L179","doc":"The Reeb derivation `ξ : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.forms","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L177-L177","doc":"The object of 1-forms `Ω¹(A)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.A","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L175-L175","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.mk","kind":"ctor","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L172-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb","kind":"structure","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L171-L195","doc":"Mirror of `categorical-reeb.lean`'s `CategoricalReeb`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-reeb","label":"def:categorical-reeb","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_V_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_V_idem","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L169-L169","doc":"Idempotency of vertical projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_H_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_H_idem","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L167-L167","doc":"Idempotency of horizontal projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.complementary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.complementary","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L165-L165","doc":"Complementarity: `π_H + π_V = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_V","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L163-L163","doc":"The vertical projection `π_V : Ω^k(A) → Ω^k(A)` (non-zero weight). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_H","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L161-L161","doc":"The horizontal projection `π_H : Ω^k(A) → Ω^k(A)` (weight-0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.forms","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L159-L159","doc":"The object of `k`-forms `Ω^k(A)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L156-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L155-L169","doc":"Mirror of `weight-decomposition.lean`'s `WeightDecomposition`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:weight-decomposition","label":"def:weight-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.quantum_regime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.quantum_regime","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L139-L144","doc":"For q > 1, the vertical weight is positive (quantum regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L134-L137","doc":"At q = 1, the interpolated differential equals the full differential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.mk'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.mk'","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L126-L132","doc":"Construct the interpolated differential from q₀ > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.coeff_full_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.coeff_full_eq","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L124-L124","doc":"coeff_full = q₀⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.sum_to_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.sum_to_one","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L122-L122","doc":"The coefficients sum to 1 (convex combination). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.coeff_vert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.coeff_vert","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L120-L120","doc":"Weight on the vertical projection: 1 − q₀⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.coeff_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.coeff_full","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L118-L118","doc":"Weight on the full differential: q₀⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential.mk","kind":"ctor","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InterpolatedDifferential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InterpolatedDifferential","kind":"structure","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L100-L124","doc":"The interpolated differential operator `d_q` at parameter `q₀`.\n\nGiven the Reeb data (d, π_V) from a `CategoricalReeb` structure,\nthe interpolated operator is:\n\n  `d_q(f) = q₀⁻¹ · d(f) + (1 − q₀⁻¹) · π_V(d(f))`\n\nThis is encoded as a pair of scalar coefficients:\n- `coeff_full = q₀⁻¹` (weight on the full differential)\n- `coeff_vert = 1 − q₀⁻¹ = ℏ_q` (weight on the vertical projection)\n\nThe operator is well-defined because:\n- The Reeb decomposition provides d and π_V\n- The weight decomposition ensures π_H + π_V = id\n- At q₀ = 1: coeff_full = 1, coeff_vert = 0, so d_q = d\n- As q₀ → ∞: coeff_full → 0, coeff_vert → 1, so d_q → π_V ∘ d ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.ofConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.ofConstant","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L82-L98","doc":"**Existence of the substrate parameter** (constant field).\n\nGiven `q₀ > 1` that is not a root of unity (e.g., `q₀`\ntranscendental), the constant field `q(p) = q₀` defines a valid\n`SubstrateParameter M` for any type `M`.\n\nThis is the simplest constructor; non-constant substrate fields\narise from the Reeb flow parameterisation.\n\nRef: [kock2004] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L40-L41","doc":"The inverse indeterminate `q⁻¹` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L37-L38","doc":"The canonical indeterminate `q` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean#L33-L35","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}